# ldap-missing-from-seeds.ldif — the entries the live directory holds that no seed LDIF creates.
#
# Measured 2026-09-18 by diffing the running directory against every *.ldif in this folder: 84 entries
# live, 65 seeded, 25 unseeded — 6 people and 18 groups (plus one container). They were added to the
# directory by hand while the dashboard's features were built, so a rebuild from the seeds alone produced
# a cluster whose LDAP users the tests and screenshots refer to but the directory does not have.
#
# userPassword is deliberately absent: these are development accounts and this file is in git. Set them
# after import, the way 20-import-ldap-data.sh does for the seeded people:
#   ldappasswd -x -H ldap://localhost:389 -D "cn=admin,dc=ephico2real,dc=com" -w "$LDAP_ADMIN_PASSWORD" \
#              -s '<the development password>' "uid=<user>,ou=People,dc=ephico2real,dc=com"
#
# Apply after 20-import-ldap-data.sh:
#   oc exec -i -n ldap-testing deploy/openldap-server -- ldapadd -x \
#     -D "cn=admin,dc=ephico2real,dc=com" -w "$LDAP_ADMIN_PASSWORD" < ldap-missing-from-seeds.ldif

